                <pb facs="0553" n="545" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg545"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.516/249: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bullitt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-10-09T19:00:00-05:00">October 9, 1939—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1201. Your 2376, October 7, 3 p.m. Circular instruction being sent through Bern.
                    You will of course not send true readings of code messages to Consuls by
                    mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
